  "title": "Brain-wide human sEEG during aversive eyepuffs and ketamine infusion (Kauvar, Richman, Liu et al. 2025; DANDI 001347)",
  "description": "This dataset provides stereo-EEG (sEEG) recordings from seven adult epilepsy patients undergoing extended-stay clinical monitoring. The recordings capture brain-wide responses to brief aversive air puffs to the eye and the modulation of those responses by a 40-minute ketamine infusion (0.5 mg/kg). It is a BIDS-iEEG derivative of the authors' NWB release (DANDI 001347), covering 30 recordings of 20 minutes each at 200 Hz, with contacts labelled anatomically but without coordinates.",
  "methods_description": "sEEG was recorded with a Nihon Kohden JE-120 amplifier from clinically placed AdTech depth electrodes. The authors applied an FIR anti-aliasing low-pass filter, downsampled to 200 Hz, and cut 20-minute windows around the start of the eyepuff series. The NWB data were converted to BrainVision float32 microvolts for BIDS-iEEG, with no further filtering, resampling or re-referencing.",
